[[File:Map040.png|center|350px]]
'''Garden of Wilted Thoughts''' (枯れた思考の庭, ''Kareta Shikō no Niwa'', '''Garden of Withered Thoughts''') is the 9th sub-chapter of [[Zero Legends]], and the 107th sub-chapter overall. It was introduced in [[Version 13.1 Update|Version 13.1]] and is available up to {{2c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
This sub-chapter is somewhat similar to [[Depths of My Heart]] in that it has relatively easy stages overall, except for the final stage, which drops a [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] and is nearly impossible without insane amounts of strategy or powerful [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating units]] such as [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Rapper Cat]] or a high-level [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]].

[[Forest of Irony]] is the easiest stage in the sub-chapter, whilst by far, the hardest stage is [[Adherence to Virtue]].
{{LegendDiff|120}}

==New Features==
The [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy type is introduced here. Sage is a unique typing that works like [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], but also has the gimmick of 70% resistance to debuffs inflicted by [[Cat Units]] that lack the [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayer]] ability.

This sub-chapter introduces 3 enemies to Zero Legends:
*[[Haterbaa 2.0]]: A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of [[Baa Baa]] from the [[Lovesick Again (Monthly Event)|Lovesick Again]] event. A peon that has low health, but rapidly dishes out strong, single-target strikes.
*[[Red Cyclone]]: A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] from [[Crimson Catastrophe]]. Basically a much deadlier [[One Horn]], it has high health and attacks non-stop, dealing lethal damage from point-blank range.
*[[Sage of Mind Soractes]]: A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy with fast movement speed and attack rate. He boasts an enormous 34k DPS and four million health. On top of that, he has an effective range of 430 and a 30% chance to [[Freeze]] Cats, making him a very potent first boss for Zero Legends.

This sub-chapter also includes a new obtainable unit, [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]]. He has a 30% chance to drop from the final stage (100% if a [[Treasure Radar]] is used).

