==Trivia==
*Garden of Wilted Thoughts is the last of the 8 [[Zero Legends]] sub-chapters to use a jumbled up and mirrored map of Japan, the first being [[The Edge of Spacetime]]. These 8 sub-chapters have a combined total of 48 stages, just like a [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapter]]; the 48th stage, [[Adherence to Virtue]], even has a unique [[Sage of Mind Soractes|boss]] and [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|reward]].
**These sub-chapters may specifically represent the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]] of [[Empire of Cats]], which takes place across the 47 prefectures of Japan and [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] rather than various countries and the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]]. Soractes can be seen as a foil to the first Iriomote Island boss [[The Face]], in a few ways, namely being a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] midranger who is fast and faceless rather than being slow and nothing but a face.
*Garden of Wilted Thoughts' Japanese name, Kareta Shikō no Niwa (枯れた思考の庭, "Garden of Withered Thoughts"), is a possible reference to [[wikipedia:Gunpei Yokoi|Gunpei Yokoi]]'s famous philosophy, Kareta Gijutsu no Suihei Shikō (枯れた技術の水平思考, "Lateral Thinking of Withered Technology").
*Since it's in the same sub-chapter as the [[wikipedia:Socrates|Socrates]]-inspired Sage of Mind Soractes, [[Forest of Irony]] may refer to [[wikipedia:Socratic irony|Socratic irony]].

